.TH EUCLID-CLI-EAP-DELETE-APPLICATION 1 "September 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eap-delete-application \- delete an application definition
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli eap delete-application
.BR \-\-application\-id | \-n
.I NAME
.SH DESCRIPTION
Deletes an application definition. Any instances the manager is running
are stopped on its next reconcile, a few seconds later - an application
that no longer exists is not something it keeps running.
.PP
The technical principal created for the application, if it has one, is
deleted with it, so no credential outlives what it was issued to. A user
named with
.B \-\-user
at creation is yours, and is left alone.
.PP
The artifact in the bucket is left alone too, as is the copy the manager
materialised on the host. Creating an application of the same name again
starts from that same artifact, with a new principal and a new key.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-application\-id " " \fINAME\fR
Name of the application to delete. Required.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The definition was deleted.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the caller is not an authenticated
administrator, or no application of that name exists.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli eap delete-application --application-id demo
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eap (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eap-stop-application (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eap-create-application (1)
